  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 130 AM MDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nThe upper high will meander near or over NM through the end of the\nweek. It does appear PWATs will trend down slightly on Monday, but\nwill continue to hover at or just above an inch through the end of\nthe week. This moisture beneath the high will allow for daily\nrounds of showers and thunderstorms, favoring the northern and\nwestern mountains through at least Thursday. An outflow boundary\nmay push into northeast NM on Friday which will increase chances\nfor thunderstorm activity there. The moisture combined with \ncontinued slow storm motions will allow for localized heavy \nrainfall, and couldn't rule out a few flash floods throughout the \nweek. Additionally, temperatures will remain hot. Triple digit \nheat is on tap for the Rio Grande Valley and eastern NM each day. \nHeat Advisories will also be likely.",
